# rendered compositor frames (.github/scripts/render-desktop.sh, which does
# `mkdir -p shots` at the repo root and writes shots/$label-$size.png there).
#
# ANCHORED. Written as a bare `shots/` it matched a directory of that name at
# ANY depth, which is not what the line above describes and not what it was for:
# it also swallowed `docs/shots/`, where the two reference screenshots for
# POINTER-PROMPT.md 1c live. Those are evidence, not output - the "before" one
# cannot be regenerated at all, because the branch that drew it has never been
# identified - so an ignore rule aimed at CI output must not reach them.
/shots/
kernel/tests/host/wmbench

# clangd's index and Cursor's per-worktree state. Machine-local, never shared.
.cache/
.cursor/
examples/Zaccoding.zl
